---
// Website terms of use, plus a short summary of how quotes and work are handled.
// DRAFT: to be reviewed by the business (ideally with a solicitor) before relying on it.
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

const updated = '12 October 2026';
const mail = `mailto:${site.email}`;
---

<PageLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms of use for the Eclipse Shield website, and how our quotes and work are handled."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  heading="Terms of use"
  intro={`Last updated ${updated}.`}
>
  <h2>About us</h2>
  <p>
    This website is run by {site.legalName}, a company registered in {site.registeredIn} with company number
    {' '}{site.companyNumber}{site.registeredOffice ? `, registered office ${site.registeredOffice}` : ''}. You can
    contact us at <a href={mail}>{site.email}</a>{site.phone && <> or on {site.phone}</>}.
  </p>
  <p>By using this website you agree to these terms. If you don’t agree, please don’t use the site.</p>

  <h2>Using this website</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You can use this website free of charge to find out about our services and contact us.</li>
    <li>
      We may update, change or suspend the website at any time. We aim to keep it available but can’t promise it will
      always be.
    </li>
    <li>
      Please don’t misuse the site, for example by sending spam through the quote form, trying to get unauthorised
      access, or introducing anything harmful.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Information on this website</h2>
  <p>
    The information on this website is general information about window film. It isn’t advice for your particular
    windows. How a film performs depends on things like the type of glass, which way the window faces and how the room
    is used. We confirm which film is suitable for your glass when we survey or quote for your job.
  </p>
  <p>
    We try to keep the information accurate and up to date, but we can’t guarantee it is always complete or current.
  </p>

  <h2>Quotes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Quotes are free and come with no obligation.</li>
    <li>
      A quote is based on the information and photos you give us, or on what we see at a survey. If the job turns out
      to be different, for example the glass type or access, we will tell you and confirm any change before going
      ahead.
    </li>
    <li>Each quote says how long it is valid for.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Work we carry out</h2>
  <p>
    Any work is carried out under the terms in your written quote or agreement, which will set out the price, what is
    included and any guarantee on the film and fitting. If anything in your quote differs from these terms, the quote
    applies.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are a consumer, you have legal rights, including that our work is carried out with reasonable care and
    skill. If you agree a contract with us at your home or remotely (for example by phone or email), you normally have
    14 days to cancel. If you ask us to start work within those 14 days and then cancel, you may have to pay for work
    already done. Nothing in these terms affects your legal rights.
  </p>

  <h2>Our content</h2>
  <p>
    The text, photos, logo and design of this website belong to {site.legalName} or are used with permission. Please
    don’t copy or reuse them without asking us first.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>Where we link to other websites, we aren’t responsible for their content or how they use your information.</p>

  <h2>Our responsibility to you</h2>
  <p>
    We don’t exclude or limit our liability where it would be unlawful to do so, including for death or personal
    injury caused by our negligence, or for fraud. We are not responsible for losses from using this website that we
    couldn’t reasonably have foreseen, or for business losses arising from use of the website.
  </p>

  <h2>Your personal information</h2>
  <p>How we use personal information is explained in our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms from time to time. The date at the top shows when they were last changed.</p>

  <h2>Law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales. If you live in Scotland or Northern Ireland, you can also
    bring proceedings in your local courts.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
